## Summary Table: Repair Subsystem Coverage

| Layer | Healthy | Degraded | Corrupt | Recoverable | Verified |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Cool** | All readable, no sentinels | Schema mismatch | Unreadable fragment | Yes (migrate or re-run) | `verify_cool()` ✓ |
| **Warm** | `bathos.db` valid, full row count | Rows missing (compaction pending) | Header or structure corrupted | Yes (`force-rebuild`) | `verify_warm()` ✓ |
| **Archive** | All partitions present + checksums match | Manifest old (schema < 2) | File missing or SHA256 mismatch | Partial (re-archive, quarantine) | `verify_archive()` ✓ |
| **Sync** | All fragments complete | (N/A during sync) | Truncated fragment on dest | Yes (delete + re-pull) | Post-pull scan ✓ |
| **Lock** | No lock file | Lock present + PID active | Lock stale (PID gone) | Yes (auto-cleanup) | `compact()` checks ✓ |

This PEGS map is **exhaustive and concrete**, anchored to the code at `path:line` and structured for direct input to the brainstorming/spec-writing phase.
